1. PREREQUISITES ON THE SERVER
----------------------------------------------------------
# Docker access for your user (this was the blocker before)
sudo usermod -aG docker $USER
# then log out and log back in, and check:
docker ps

# Install minikube
curl -LO https://storage.googleapis.com/minikube/releases/latest/minikube-linux-amd64
sudo install minikube-linux-amd64 /usr/local/bin/minikube
minikube version

# kubectl (skip if already installed)
kubectl version --client

# Resources: the deploy script starts minikube with 2 CPUs and 4 GB of memory,
# which is enough for the 6 pods.


2. DEPLOY
----------------------------------------------------------
cd 2025MT03083_FoodExpress
./deployment/deploy-minikube.sh     # starts minikube, enables dashboard + metrics-server,
                                    # builds both images with `minikube image build`, applies manifests,
                                    # waits for all rollouts
./deployment/smoke-test.sh          # end-to-end calls (run on the server)

# Check
kubectl -n foodexpress get deployments,pods,svc,hpa -o wide


3. REACHING THE SERVICES FROM YOUR LAPTOP (POSTMAN)
----------------------------------------------------------
The minikube IP (e.g. 192.168.49.2) is only reachable from inside the server.

Option A - port-forward on the server:
  kubectl -n foodexpress port-forward --address 0.0.0.0 svc/restaurant-service 3001:3001 &
  kubectl -n foodexpress port-forward --address 0.0.0.0 svc/order-service 3002:3002 &

  In Postman set:
    restaurantUrl = http://<server-ip>:3001
    orderUrl      = http://<server-ip>:3002

Option B - if the server's firewall blocks those ports, start the same
port-forwards on the server, then open an SSH tunnel from your laptop:
  ssh -L 3001:localhost:3001 -L 3002:localhost:3002 <user>@<server>

  In Postman set:
    restaurantUrl = http://localhost:3001
    orderUrl      = http://localhost:3002

Import: postman/2025MT03083_Ajeet_Kumar_Yadav_FoodExpress.postman_collection.json


4. OPENING THE KUBERNETES DASHBOARD FROM YOUR LAPTOP
----------------------------------------------------------
# On the server (do not let it try to open a browser there):
minikube dashboard --url
#   prints: http://127.0.0.1:<port>/api/v1/namespaces/kubernetes-dashboard/services/http:kubernetes-dashboard:/proxy/

# On your laptop:
ssh -L <port>:localhost:<port> <user>@<server>

# Open the printed URL in your laptop's browser, then choose namespace "foodexpress".


